choc-webview2-external-drop.patch: the WebView2 backend can turn off drops
that come from outside the web view (B448 C3, ADR-205 item 3).

Base:     choc a08bfd84494921700703a8433b9d1a304edfafd2 (the libs/choc pin)
Applied:  at configure time, to a build-tree copy of libs/choc/choc, by
          libs/patches/apply_patch.cmake, after choc-webview2-navigation.patch
          and choc-webview2-permissions.patch. The submodule is never edited.
Checked:  tools/choc_patch_check.py (./verify fast).

PURPOSE. WebView2 has a native switch for content dragged in from outside the
view, ICoreWebView2Controller4::put_AllowExternalDrop. An app cannot reach it
through choc: the controller is private, and choc declares only
ICoreWebView2Controller and ICoreWebView2Controller2. This adds one option,
WebView::Options::allowExternalDrop, and the two interface declarations the
call needs. horde's Windows backend (src/gui/hypersaw_gui_win.cpp) sets it to
false. It is a second layer: both shipped pages already refuse dragenter,
dragover and drop (tools/gui_sink_check.py), and the navigation rule already
stops a drop from navigating the view. On macOS the backend unregisters the
view's dragged types instead (hypersaw_gui.mm).

DEFAULT UNCHANGED. The patch only adds lines. The option defaults to true,
which is WebView2's own default, and the new block runs only when the option
is false: left at its default, no interface is queried and nothing is called,
so the controller is set up exactly as upstream.

INTERFACES. Declarations follow WebView2.h in Microsoft's WebView2 SDK (NuGet
package Microsoft.Web.WebView2, build/native/include/WebView2.h; read from
version 1.0.2903.40):
  ICoreWebView2Controller3  f9614724-5d2b-41dc-aef7-73d62b51543b
      : public ICoreWebView2Controller2. Eight methods, in the SDK's order:
      get/put_RasterizationScale, get/put_ShouldDetectMonitorScaleChanges,
      add/remove_RasterizationScaleChanged, get/put_BoundsMode.
  ICoreWebView2Controller4  97d418d5-a426-4e49-a151-e1a10f327d9e
      : public ICoreWebView2Controller3. get_AllowExternalDrop,
      put_AllowExternalDrop.
Controller3 is declared only because Controller4 derives from it: its eight
methods fill the vtable slots ahead of Controller4's, and a missing or
reordered one would make put_AllowExternalDrop call the wrong slot. Its event
handler is declared void* and COREWEBVIEW2_BOUNDS_MODE as an empty enum, as
choc does for the types it never uses; neither method is called.
tools/choc_patch_check.py holds the two IIDs and the method order, and is red
if the patched header differs.

OLDER RUNTIME. Where the installed WebView2 runtime does not provide
ICoreWebView2Controller4, QueryInterface fails, nothing is called, and the
view is created as before. The page's own guard still applies there.

SEPARATE FILE. It is carried apart from the navigation and permission patches
so that each can be dropped when upstream takes its part. It is made against
the pristine pin and changes no line their hunks rely on, so it applies alone
and in any order with them; tools/choc_patch_check.py checks every order.

UPSTREAM STATUS. Not yet proposed. A feature request for the option is
drafted for the human's review (choc takes feature requests as issues, not
pull requests; its CONTRIBUTING.md); posting it outside the fleet takes the
human's explicit yes.

REMOVAL CONDITION. Delete this patch and its wiring (libs/patches/README.md
lists every piece) when the pinned choc provides an equivalent option. If the
upstream shape differs, port src/gui/hypersaw_gui_win.cpp to it in the same
change. Any bump of libs/choc turns tools/choc_patch_check.py red until the
Base line above is updated, so the question is asked at every bump.

--- a/choc/gui/choc_WebView.h
+++ b/choc/gui/choc_WebView.h
@@ -80,6 +80,15 @@
         /// webview to be used as input, rather than the default behaviour, which is
         /// for the first click to give the webview focus but not trigger any action.
         bool acceptsFirstMouseClick = false;
+
+        /// Where supported, setting this to false stops the webview accepting
+        /// content dragged in from outside it and dropped on it (for example a
+        /// file from the desktop, or a link from another application). The
+        /// default, true, leaves the browser's own behaviour unchanged.
+        /// Currently implemented by the WebView2 (Windows) backend, where the
+        /// installed runtime provides ICoreWebView2Controller4; on a runtime
+        /// without it, false has no effect.
+        bool allowExternalDrop = true;
 
         /// Optional user-agent string which can be used to override the default. Leave
         // this empty for default behaviour.
@@ -1267,6 +1276,35 @@
     static IID getIID()     { return { 0xc979903e, 0xd4ca, 0x4228, { 0x92, 0xeb, 0x47, 0xee, 0x3f, 0xa9, 0x6e, 0xab } }; }
 
 };
+
+// ICoreWebView2Controller3 is declared only because ICoreWebView2Controller4
+// derives from it: its eight methods fill the vtable slots ahead of
+// Controller4's, so all eight must be here, in the SDK's order. Both
+// declarations follow WebView2.h in Microsoft's WebView2 SDK (NuGet package
+// Microsoft.Web.WebView2, build/native/include/WebView2.h).
+enum COREWEBVIEW2_BOUNDS_MODE {};
+
+MIDL_INTERFACE("f9614724-5d2b-41dc-aef7-73d62b51543b")
+ICoreWebView2Controller3 : public ICoreWebView2Controller2
+{
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE get_RasterizationScale(double*) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE put_RasterizationScale(double) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE get_ShouldDetectMonitorScaleChanges(BOOL*) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE put_ShouldDetectMonitorScaleChanges(BOOL) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE add_RasterizationScaleChanged(void*, EventRegistrationToken*) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE remove_RasterizationScaleChanged(EventRegistrationToken) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE get_BoundsMode(COREWEBVIEW2_BOUNDS_MODE*) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE put_BoundsMode(COREWEBVIEW2_BOUNDS_MODE) = 0;
+};
+
+MIDL_INTERFACE("97d418d5-a426-4e49-a151-e1a10f327d9e")
+ICoreWebView2Controller4 : public ICoreWebView2Controller3
+{
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE get_AllowExternalDrop(BOOL*) = 0;
+    virtual HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE put_AllowExternalDrop(BOOL) = 0;
+
+    static IID getIID()     { return { 0x97d418d5, 0xa426, 0x4e49, { 0xa1, 0x51, 0xe1, 0xa1, 0x0f, 0x32, 0x7d, 0x9e } }; }
+};
 
 STDAPI CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentWithOptions(PCWSTR, PCWSTR, void*, ICoreWebView2CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentCompletedHandler*);
 
@@ -1472,6 +1510,20 @@
                 controller2->put_DefaultBackgroundColor ({ 0, 0, 0, 0 });
             }
         }
+
+        // Only when the option is turned off: left at its default, nothing is called.
+        if (! options.allowExternalDrop)
+        {
+            COMPtr<ICoreWebView2Controller4> controller4;
+
+            // A runtime without Controller4 fails this query, and external drops
+            // then stay as the runtime has them.
+            if (controller->QueryInterface (ICoreWebView2Controller4::getIID(), (void**) controller4.getAddress()) == S_OK
+                  && controller4 != nullptr)
+            {
+                controller4->put_AllowExternalDrop (FALSE);
+            }
+        }
 
         auto wildcardFilter = createUTF16StringFromUTF8 (defaultURI + "*");
         coreWebView->AddWebResourceRequestedFilter (wildcardFilter.c_str(), COREWEBVIEW2_WEB_RESOURCE_CONTEXT_ALL);
